255	
256	  // CodeRabbit (SFCC-11 cumulative review): product-quantity-picker.tsx's handleQuantityChange
257	  // unconditionally calls `.then(...)` on onItemQuantityChange's return value. The old default,
258	  // `noop`, returned undefined synchronously - `undefined.then` throws before this test's key
259	  // handler even finishes. This proves a caller that omits the prop entirely can still actually
260	  // change the quantity without throwing, not just that rendering alone doesn't throw.
